; WILDCARD_FALSE_POSITIVE, authoritative-signal path.
;
; The unsigned fixture (zones/unsigned/wildcard.test.zone) covers behavioural
; detection: probe a random label and see whether it also answers. That works
; everywhere but costs an extra query and is inferential.
;
; On a signed zone there is a definitive signal instead. RRSIG carries a `Labels`
; field holding the label count of the *original* owner name, so a wildcard-
; synthesized answer has Labels smaller than the queried name's label count.
; Two detection paths need two fixtures, or one of them ships untested.
$ORIGIN wildcard-signed.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.

; Signed wildcard. A query for anything.wildcard-signed.test returns an RRSIG
; with Labels=2 while the queried name has 3 labels.
*       IN TXT  "signed-wildcard-synthesized"

; Explicitly present, so Labels matches the query and no false positive is raised.
real    IN TXT  "signed-and-genuinely-present"
